From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: conda-forge nodejs-feedstock <noreply@conda-forge.org>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Explicitly instantiate FloatMinMaxHelper on RISC-V

MacroAssembler::FloatMinMaxHelper is declared in macro-assembler-riscv.h but
defined in macro-assembler-riscv.cc, and maglev-ir-riscv.cc calls it directly
from another translation unit. Within macro-assembler-riscv.cc the only uses
are the four Float32Max/Min and Float64Max/Min wrappers; at -O3 GCC inlines all
of them and discards the out-of-line instantiations, so nothing satisfies
maglev's references and the link of node_mksnapshot fails:

  riscv64-conda-linux-gnu-ld: maglev-ir-riscv.o: in function
    'v8::internal::maglev::Float64Min::GenerateCode(...)':
  undefined reference to 'void
    v8::internal::MacroAssembler::FloatMinMaxHelper<double>(
      v8::internal::FPURegister, v8::internal::FPURegister,
      v8::internal::FPURegister, v8::internal::MaxMinKind)'

Add explicit instantiation definitions for both specializations so they are
always emitted with external linkage. This affects the RISC-V backend only.
---
 deps/v8/src/codegen/riscv/macro-assembler-riscv.cc | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

--- a/deps/v8/src/codegen/riscv/macro-assembler-riscv.cc
+++ b/deps/v8/src/codegen/riscv/macro-assembler-riscv.cc
@@ -7245,6 +7245,28 @@
   bind(&done);
 }
 
+// FloatMinMaxHelper is declared in macro-assembler-riscv.h but defined here,
+// and maglev-ir-riscv.cc calls it directly from another translation unit. The
+// implicit instantiations produced by the four wrappers below are not enough:
+// the compiler inlines every use within this file and is free to discard the
+// out-of-line copies, which leaves maglev's references undefined at link time:
+//
+//   maglev-ir-riscv.o: in function 'v8::internal::maglev::Float64Min::GenerateCode(...)'
+//   undefined reference to 'void v8::internal::MacroAssembler::FloatMinMaxHelper<double>(
+//       v8::internal::FPURegister, v8::internal::FPURegister,
+//       v8::internal::FPURegister, v8::internal::MaxMinKind)'
+//
+// Instantiate both specializations explicitly so the definitions are always
+// emitted with external linkage.
+template void MacroAssembler::FloatMinMaxHelper<float>(FPURegister dst,
+                                                       FPURegister src1,
+                                                       FPURegister src2,
+                                                       MaxMinKind kind);
+template void MacroAssembler::FloatMinMaxHelper<double>(FPURegister dst,
+                                                        FPURegister src1,
+                                                        FPURegister src2,
+                                                        MaxMinKind kind);
+
 void MacroAssembler::Float32Max(FPURegister dst, FPURegister src1,
                                 FPURegister src2) {
   ASM_CODE_COMMENT(this);
